# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: partial monomorphization instantiates opaque generic items with their contents
#
# Under --monomorphize-mut, a generic function (or closure method, defaulted method, or a type
# partial monomorphization specializes) that an --opaque pattern makes opaque keeps its translated
# contents. The instances partial monomorphization creates for the `&mut` arguments used by this
# crate are transparent and keep the body (or fields); the generic item itself is made opaque again
# after the pass. This lets a separately translated chunk list the items of earlier chunks as opaque
# and still get bodies for the instances it needs. #[charon::opaque] items stay opaque. UI test
# monomorphize-mut-opaque.

